From 1a844862eb82c601463521c2d5ad17a7cb05beaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:38:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix slow splash/login/logout, add instant-feedback logout,
 premium home header

Root causes of the 60+ second loading:
- AppConfig had 30s timeouts x 3 retries at 2s/4s/8s backoff - a single
  endpoint that kept timing out could take up to ~134 seconds worst case.
  Trimmed to 12-15s timeouts x 2 retries at 1s/2s backoff (~39s worst case),
  appropriate for a still-generous-but-not-punishing background retry,
  rather than something a user sits through in the critical boot path.
- splash_screen.dart ran the force-update version check and the session
  check sequentially - two separate network round trips stacked on top of
  a flat 1800ms artificial delay. Now both are started before either is
  awaited (so they run concurrently), and the 1800ms is a floor rather than
  something added on top of network time.
- AuthRepositoryImpl.logout() awaited the remote /auth/logout call BEFORE
  clearing the local session - meaning the entire logout, as far as the UI
  was concerned, was gated behind a network round trip that could itself
  take up to ~40s on a bad connection, with no loading indicator shown
  while it happened. Local session clear now happens first and is awaited;
  the backend notification fires in the background and its result is
  ignored, since the tokens are already gone locally regardless of whether
  it succeeds.
- profile_screen.dart's sign-out confirmation dialog closed immediately on
  tap with zero visual feedback while the (now much faster) logout ran.
  Now shows an inline spinner on the button and stays open until it
  completes.

Also: new AppColors.premiumGradient (gold-to-black, matching the splash
screen) applied to the home screen's header section (avatar/greeting bar +
wallet card), which already uses gold tones itself via
AppColors.walletGradient - the rest of the page (quick actions,
transactions) is intentionally left on the existing light background to
avoid a wholesale reskin risking readability regressions across a screen
that large; this can be extended further on request.

Could not run flutter analyze/build in this sandbox (no network path to
the Dart SDK download host) - verified by close manual review and brace/
paren balancing instead; please run flutter analyze before merging.
